    "result_text": "I've implemented `publish_run` in `app/publish.py` and all 3 tests pass. The tests use a fake API object, so nothing has been run against the real Hugging Face Hub yet.\n\n**Which upload method I used:** in the pinned huggingface_hub 2.0.0, `upload_large_folder` is deprecated. The docs and the installed source now say plain `HfApi.upload_folder` handles very large folders when `hf_xet` is installed, and `hf_xet` 1.6.0 is already in the venv. It splits the upload into several commits so it stays under the Hub's file-count limits. If a job dies halfway, calling it again skips files already committed and doesn't re-send data already uploaded. So `publish_run`:\n\n1. calls `api.create_repo(repo_id, repo_type=\"dataset\", private=True, exist_ok=True)`. This creates a private repo if needed, and does nothing if the repo already exists.\n2. calls `api.upload_folder(...)` on `run_dir` with no `path_in_repo`, so the folder layout lands at the root of the repo. It skips `*.tmp` and `wandb/*`.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- The patterns work on nested paths, because in this library's matching `*` also matches `/`. So `ckpt/step-100/model.safetensors.tmp` and anything under `wandb/` are skipped. A new test checks this with the library's own filter function.\n- Only the `wandb/` folder at the top of `run_dir` is skipped. A `wandb/` folder deeper down would still be uploaded; tell me if you want that excluded too.\n- The resume behaviour depends on `hf_xet` staying installed. Without it, `upload_folder` falls back to a single commit, which can't resume.\n- Like `publish_summary`, the function takes an optional `api` argument so tests can pass in a fake.\n\nI also added two tests to `tests/test_publish.py`: one checks the repo-creation and upload calls, the other checks the skip patterns."
  },
